# Variants are values, not lookup keys

Pass the **variant object** (border, background, badge, …) into viewers.
Do **not** pass a string name and look it up in a shared `VARIANT_CHROME` /
`VARIANT_MAP`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — key + all-styles-knowing map; viewer depends on the map
type VariantName = "default" | "followUp";
const VARIANT_CHROME: Record<VariantName, Chrome> = { … };
viewer: ({ variant }) => <div style={{ color: VARIANT_CHROME[variant].fg }} />
<Item variant="followUp" />

// ✅ GOOD — variant is the chrome itself
type Variant = { fg: string; border: string; background: string; badge: ReactNode };
viewer: ({ variant }) => <div style={{ color: variant.fg }} />
<Item variant={followUpChrome} />
```

## Why

A name-key forces every consumer to share one map that knows every style.
Passing the value keeps chrome host-owned and removes that dependency.

## Phase bags are dicts of values

The host **builds** a dictionary of Variant objects. The **library** picks
`bag[state][type]` and passes that object into the viewer. Hosts do not
supply `resolveVariant` or dual `variants` / `followUpVariants` bags.

| Phase | Prop | Library pick |
|---|---|---|
| Design | `variants: Variants` | `variants[type]` |
| Fill | `variants: Record<ResponderState, Variants>` | `variants[state][type]` |
| Review | `variants: Record<ReviewVariantState, Variants>` | `variants[state][type]` |

`ResponderState`: `default` \| `old` \| `change` \| `error`.
`ReviewVariantState`: `default` \| `change`.
`Variant` stays **per type** (`Variants[K]` can differ across `field` / `heading` / …).

```typescript
// ✅ Host constructs the Record; library picks by status
const responderVariants: Record<ResponderState, Variants> = {
  default: defaultChrome,
  old: defaultChrome,
  change: followUpChrome,
  error: defaultChrome,
};
<FormResponder variants={responderVariants} />

// ❌ BAD — host resolver reaching into chrome maps
resolveVariant={(item) =>
  pending ? followUpVariants[item.type] : defaultVariants[item.type]
}
```

Storybook controls may still use name keys **at the host boundary** only —
map `TEXT_VARIANT[controlName]` before passing into viewers.

Picking `bag[status]` inside the library is not the anti-pattern: the
anti-pattern is a **second** map from name → style that viewers must import.
